WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.008 --> 00:00:14.051
It was nearly daybreak.

2
00:00:15.011 --> 00:00:18.993
Wrapped in a coverlet, Fagin crouched over a cold hearth in the kitchen of his lair.

3
00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:23.054
Bolter was stretched out upon a mattress on the floor, fast asleep.

4
00:00:24.114 --> 00:00:25.615
Fagin was thinking about Nancy.

5
00:00:26.615 --> 00:00:27.855
She had talked to strangers!

6
00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:31.424
She still loved Bill Sikes!

7
00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:34.445
Fagin was full of rage and full of fear that he might be arrested.

8
00:00:35.366 --> 00:00:38.327
But his vengeful thoughts were interrupted by a knock at the front door.

9
00:00:39.407 --> 00:00:43.629
Fagin crept upstairs and soon returned with a man hidden under a large coat and scarf.

10
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.471
Sitting down and throwing off his outer garments, the man revealed himself as Sikes.

11
00:00:48.491 --> 00:00:52.173
"There!" said Sikes, laying a bundle on the table.

12
00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:53.893
"Take care of that.

13
00:00:54.914 --> 00:00:56.134
It's been trouble enough to get."

14
00:00:57.135 --> 00:00:59.996
Fagin took the bundle of stolen goods and locked them up in a cupboard.

15
00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:04.093
"I'm glad to see you're well enough to be working again, Bill.

16
00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.495
I only hope you're well enough to hear a bit of news."

17
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.375
"What news?"

18
00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.376
Sikes was instantly suspicious.

19
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.497
Fagin gestured toward the sleeping Bolter.

20
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:18.939
"Let's say that this lad here was ready to inform on all of us.

21
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.321
That first he sought out the right folks and then he described us to them.

22
00:01:24.342 --> 00:01:27.823
That no one forced him to do this, but he did it because he wanted to.

23
00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:29.684
What would you do?"

24
00:01:30.812 --> 00:01:32.313
"Why, I'd beat him to death!"

25
00:01:32.793 --> 00:01:34.094
Sikes responded immediately.

26
00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:36.935
"And what if Charley or the Dodger did it?"

27
00:01:37.316 --> 00:01:38.176
Fagin pressed on.

28
00:01:39.197 --> 00:01:40.097
"What if I did it?"

29
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:44.239
"It doesn't matter who did it," replied Sikes, clenching his teeth.

30
00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:46.661
"I'd kill them in an instant.

31
00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:48.762
I promise you that."

32
00:01:49.902 --> 00:01:52.384
Fagin looked at Bolter, still slumbering on the floor.

33
00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:54.785
"Poor lad.

34
00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:58.007
He's worn out from watching her so long."

35
00:01:58.027 --> 00:01:59.968
"What do you mean?"

36
00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:01.153
Sikes demanded.

37
00:02:02.194 --> 00:02:04.296
Fagin did not answer but shook Bolter awake.

38
00:02:04.316 --> 00:02:07.198
"Tell me again what you told me before.

39
00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:09.841
Tell me so Bill can hear."

40
00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.143
Bolter stretched and yawned.

41
00:02:12.163 --> 00:02:17.407
"Tell us how Nancy went to London Bridge and met a gentleman and a lady," Fagin prompted.

42
00:02:17.427 --> 00:02:19.129
"That's right.

43
00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:20.830
That's what she did."

44
00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.613
"Tell us how she'd met the lady before.

45
00:02:24.594 --> 00:02:26.956
How the gentleman asked her to give up Monks and she did.

46
00:02:28.044 --> 00:02:30.346
Tell us how she described him and the pub where we meet.

47
00:02:31.387 --> 00:02:33.609
Tell us how she gave up everything without a threat!"

48
00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:35.771
cried Fagin, half mad with fury.

49
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:37.372
"All right."

50
00:02:38.373 --> 00:02:39.434
Bolter scratched his head.

51
00:02:39.454 --> 00:02:41.655
"That's just what she did."

52
00:02:41.675 --> 00:02:45.539
"And what did she say about last Sunday?"

53
00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:46.499
asked Fagin.

54
00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:51.884
"She said she couldn't meet them last Sunday because she'd been forcibly kept at home by Bill, the

55
00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.946
man she'd described to the lady before."

56
00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:56.628
"What else did she say about Bill?"

57
00:02:57.656 --> 00:03:01.239
"That she couldn't go outside unless he knew where she was going," Bolter said.

58
00:03:01.259 --> 00:03:06.163
"So the first time she went to see the lady, she put a sleeping potion in his drink."

59
00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:08.305
Sikes went white.

60
00:03:08.325 --> 00:03:10.207
"That woman!"

61
00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:11.107
he cried.

62
00:03:12.168 --> 00:03:16.232
Pushing Fagin aside, he rushed from the room and ran upstairs to the front door.

63
00:03:17.372 --> 00:03:20.895
Once out on the street, he did not stop until he was back at his own house.

64
00:03:22.196 --> 00:03:23.798
There he found Nancy asleep.

65
00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:28.985
Before she could cry out, he carried out the horrible promise he had made to Fagin.

66
00:03:30.066 --> 00:03:32.607
Then he called his dog, and the two of them left the house.

67
00:03:34.487 --> 00:03:35.968
Sikes spent the whole day on the run.

68
00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:39.769
He wandered for miles and still wasn't sure where he was going.

69
00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.311
At last he stopped to eat at a pub outside of London.

70
00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:45.872
But it was not a very restful meal.

71
00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.273
"Did you hear about that London murder?"

72
00:03:48.653 --> 00:03:50.054
one man in the pub asked another.

73
00:03:50.074 --> 00:03:53.315
"Such a dreadful murder," said the second man.

74
00:03:53.335 --> 00:03:55.516
"She was beaten to death."

75
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.962
"I hear the suspect ran north," said the first man.

76
00:03:58.982 --> 00:04:02.284
"It doesn't matter where he runs, the police will get him.

77
00:04:03.405 --> 00:04:04.465
Everyone is looking for him."

78
00:04:05.606 --> 00:04:08.628
Overhearing this, Sikes quickly paid his bill and left with his dog.

79
00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:12.971
That night they took shelter in a barn, but Sikes had trouble sleeping.

80
00:04:14.012 --> 00:04:16.213
Every time he closed his eyes, he saw Nancy.

81
00:04:17.214 --> 00:04:19.315
The next morning he resolved to return to London.

82
00:04:19.335 --> 00:04:22.037
"At least there will be somebody to talk to.

83
00:04:22.057 --> 00:04:26.100
"And a good hiding place too," he said to himself.

84
00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.941
"The police will never expect to find me there.

85
00:04:29.962 --> 00:04:33.044
I'll hide for a week or so, get some money from Fagin, and go to France."

86
00:04:34.285 --> 00:04:38.928
Sikes knew just where to go—a hideout near the river in a neighborhood where the warehouses stood empty.

87
00:04:40.029 --> 00:04:42.951
The houses there had long ago been abandoned by their owners too.

88
00:04:44.012 --> 00:04:47.975
But some of the houses were not empty because desperate people had broken in and were living there.

89
00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:51.577
Two such people were Toby Crackit and Charley Bates.

90
00:04:52.678 --> 00:04:55.460
They sat in an upper room of one of these ruined houses.

91
00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.737
"When was Fagin arrested?"

92
00:04:58.057 --> 00:04:58.597
asked Toby.

93
00:04:58.617 --> 00:05:01.399
"This afternoon," said Charley.

94
00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:04.061
"The Dodger and Bolter were caught too."

95
00:05:05.241 --> 00:05:06.682
Suddenly they heard a knock at the door.

96
00:05:07.783 --> 00:05:11.565
Charley peeked out the window and saw Sikes and his dog standing in the street below.

97
00:05:11.585 --> 00:05:14.567
"Bill can't be coming here!"

98
00:05:14.887 --> 00:05:15.327
he said.

99
00:05:16.428 --> 00:05:18.049
Toby ran downstairs and let him in.

100
00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:21.811
When they came upstairs, Sikes laid his hands on Toby's shoulders.

101
00:05:22.912 --> 00:05:26.377
"Toby, will you turn me in to the police, or will you let me stay here until this

102
00:05:26.397 --> 00:05:26.937
hunt is over?"

103
00:05:26.957 --> 00:05:31.398
"You may stay here if you think it's safe," said Toby after some hesitation.

104
00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:33.519
But Charley backed away.

105
00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:35.539
"I have to leave the room."

106
00:05:35.559 --> 00:05:37.280
"Why, Charley!"

107
00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:38.580
Sikes stepped toward him.

108
00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.361
"Don't you know me?"

109
00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:42.841
"Don't come any closer, you monster!

110
00:05:43.982 --> 00:05:45.062
You killed Nancy!"

111
00:05:46.182 --> 00:05:47.343
Charley clenched his fists.

112
00:05:47.363 --> 00:05:50.483
"If the police come after you, I'll give you up.

113
00:05:51.524 --> 00:05:52.424
I'm not afraid of you."

114
00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:56.374
And with that, Charley sprang at Sikes and knocked him to the ground.

115
00:05:57.375 --> 00:06:00.457
The contest was soon over as Sikes pinned Charley to the floor.

116
00:06:02.218 --> 00:06:04.120
Suddenly there was a loud knocking at the front door.

117
00:06:05.281 --> 00:06:05.681
"Open up!

118
00:06:06.742 --> 00:06:07.402
It's the police!"

119
00:06:07.782 --> 00:06:08.363
cried a voice.

120
00:06:08.383 --> 00:06:10.304
"He's in here!"

121
00:06:10.724 --> 00:06:11.385
shouted Charley.

122
00:06:11.405 --> 00:06:13.386
"Break down the door!"

123
00:06:14.527 --> 00:06:17.029
Sikes picked up Charley and flung the boy over his shoulder.

124
00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:21.152
After depositing Charley in an empty room, Sikes locked the door.

125
00:06:22.292 --> 00:06:24.473
Charley continued to yell for help from a window.

126
00:06:24.493 --> 00:06:27.354
"Twenty pounds to the man who brings a ladder!"

127
00:06:27.694 --> 00:06:28.975
shouted a policeman outside.

128
00:06:28.995 --> 00:06:30.716
"They'll kill me!"

129
00:06:31.756 --> 00:06:32.937
Sikes was panic-stricken.

130
00:06:33.917 --> 00:06:36.058
But then he spied a window at the back of the house.

131
00:06:37.098 --> 00:06:39.940
The police and a crowd of onlookers were focused on the front of the house.

132
00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:41.920
Sikes laughed.

133
00:06:42.941 --> 00:06:44.962
He climbed onto the roof and walked to the edge.

134
00:06:46.002 --> 00:06:49.804
But in an instant, he lost his balance and fell to his death.
